Fictional Band Name: Graphite Palanquin

Band Description

Graphite Palanquin is a four-member ensemble built around the idea that a signal should never arrive in exactly the same form it left.

Lin Yue — guqin, harmonics, glissandi, left-hand pressure, decay cues.
Nia Cole — Baltimore club drums, chopped breaks, relay samples, mono sub, hard-mute edits.
Wei Qian — prepared marimba, damped bars, wood percussion, contact-mic routing.
Marcus Hale — bass trumpet, cup mute, low breath tones, narrow falls, sustained pedal notes.

There is no conventional vocalist. Lin defines the harmonic field, Nia compresses or expands perceived time through restart cycles, Wei translates harmonic events into dry wooden attacks, and Marcus controls low-register tension. Live arrangements use visual cues and decay thresholds rather than backing-track section markers.

